                  "type": "boolean"
                },
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "description": "Arbitrary-precision mathematical integer lexeme. The strict JSON SourceReader must validate the raw decimal numeric token and preserve all digits before any host floating conversion. A normal host JSON.parse result may already be rounded; never use it as exact source evidence. Existing type/codec semantics govern bounds and target mapping."
                }
